<s-1 id="RM000001C3Y00PX_01_0002" proc-id="RM0550J___00001UF00000">
<ptxt>Manual Maintenance Check</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>The manual maintenance check performs a maintenance check of the in-vehicle unit (in-vehicle unit repair check and maintenance check after vehicle repair) and checks whether the member is registered with the center (at subscription, cancellation and contract change), and can switch between the emergency call enabled/disabled states.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The screen is an example display and may differ from the actual screen.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
<s2>
<ptxt>Check GPS Reception</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Check that the GPS mark is displayed on the current position screen.</ptxt>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The manual maintenance check confirms that position information can be sent accurately. Therefore, avoid locations between buildings and indoors such as in a factory, and perform it in an open location where GPS can be received.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Manual Maintenance Check</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Press the "Info G" button to display the information screen.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Press "Setup" on the information screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100944" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>On the setup screen, press and hold "HELPNET Maintenance Check" for 10 seconds or more.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100945" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connection to the center starts.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100946" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>When connected to the center, data communication is performed first, and the current position of the vehicle, the fact that a manual maintenance check is being performed, and member registration with the center are checked.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100947" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>After data communication is completed, the system enters call mode.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100948" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Talk with the center through the microphone, and check that the call can be made normally and that the reported position is correct.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100949" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>After the conversation ends, finish the check.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100950" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>If the "Confirm" button is displayed, press "Confirm".</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Then, display the current position screen.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Press the "Info G" button.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Check that the "HELPNET" switch is displayed on the information screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100937" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
<s-1 id="RM000001C3Y00PX_01_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00001UG00000">
<ptxt>Check HELPNET Call Result</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<atten4>
<ptxt>For diagnosis screen transitions, refer to HDD Navigation System - Diagnosis System (<xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000002RV02BX"/>).</ptxt>
</atten4>
<s2>
<ptxt>Diagnosis Startup</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Start diagnosis and display the diagnosis inspection menu screen. (see <xref label="Seep02" href="RM0000002RV02BX"/>)</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Select "HELPNET Check" on the diagnosis check menu screen to display the HELPNET check menu screen.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Select "Log" on the HELPNET check menu screen to display the HELPNET call log screen.</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100922" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>HELPNET Call Log</ptxt>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E100923" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<s3>
<ptxt>Check the call result.</ptxt>
<table>
<tgroup cols="2">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.45in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.68in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Item</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>Display Content</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Call Type</ptxt>
<ptxt>(*1)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Type of call</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Date/Time of Call</ptxt>
<ptxt>(*2)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays the date and time of the call as year/month/day hour:minute</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Call Result</ptxt>
<ptxt>(*3)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Displays "OK" if communication with the HELPNET operation center finished normally, and "NG" if it did not finish normally</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>"OK" displayed</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>If "NG" is displayed, perform a manual maintenance check and check whether the call can be made normally.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the manual maintenance check does not finish normally, inspect according to the instructions in the Problem Symptoms Table [Cannot connect to the center even when a manual maintenance check is performed]. (see <xref label="Seep03" href="RM000001C3P00OX"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
